<PolicyLayout title="Community Guidelines">
  <p>Help people identify bicycle components and understand their details. A clear, relevant photo is more useful than a polished advertisement.</p>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What to upload</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6"><li>Photos you took of the component named on the page, or photos you have permission to contribute.</li><li>Useful views of model markings, mounting points, construction, finish and condition.</li><li>A factual caption and an image description that helps someone who cannot see the photo.</li></ul></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Protect other people</h2><p class="mt-3">Keep the focus on the part. Crop out faces, addresses, number plates, private messages and identifying background details. Do not disclose someone else’s personal information or location. Embedded location metadata is removed, but visible clues in a photo are still visible.</p></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What is not allowed</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6"><li>Illegal content, including child sexual abuse material or anything that exploits a child.</li><li>Sexual content, threats, harassment, hate, doxxing or encouragement of harm.</li><li>Stolen photos, unlicensed manufacturer images, catalogue scans or another seller’s listing images.</li><li>Spam, advertisements, scams, deceptive captions or unrelated images.</li><li>Attempts to impersonate people, evade moderation, upload active files or interfere with the service.</li></ul></section>
  <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Review and reporting</h2><p class="mt-3">Uploads are private until approved. Moderators may ask for context, reject a submission, remove a photo or suspend an account. Use “Report this photo” for a published image, or the monitored contact below for copyright, privacy or account concerns. Explain the problem and include the photo URL.</p><p class="mt-3">Do not download, attach or redistribute suspected illegal material to make a report. If there is an immediate risk to a person, contact the appropriate emergency service or authority. If you disagree with a moderation decision, contact the operator with relevant information; please do not repost the removed content.</p></section>
</PolicyLayout>
